#4471 was filed as one known bug: the parser reads `mm/dd` and flips dates for day-first
tenants. Re-triaging the reports by **computed cause** shows the ticket holds **two** bugs,
not one. One of them has had no ticket of its own.

<Callout>
Not one bug reported many times. Two bugs, with two different fixes, merged on subject alone.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is built at render time from the export, so the counts stay honest. Intake's tag is
not the cause: it guesses from the reporter's browser the moment the report arrives, and it is
wrong often enough to hide a whole bug. The cause is computed from the tenant's locale and form.

## The two problems

**1 · parser — 379 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month-first. Every tenant
writes day-first, so `7 April` ships as `4 July`. This reaches people on every channel (app,
email, form), across all 11 tenants. This is what #4471 is really about.
Ticket: [parser reads dates month-first](https://github.com/paulklecha/mega-dev-assignments/issues/1).

**2 · hint — 33 reports.** A different bug, merged into #4471 by subject. The **booking-v3**
form prints the hint `MM/DD/YYYY`. Its tenants are day-first, so their people type the date
month-first as told, and the form stores the wrong date **at entry**, before the parser runs.
It shows up on the **form** channel only, for the three booking-v3 tenants
(`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`). Fixing the parser would not fix it.
Ticket: [booking-v3 form hint stores wrong date](https://github.com/paulklecha/mega-dev-assignments/issues/2).

## Count once, but count the right things

- The export had 427 rows; its pages overlap, so 15 were the same report twice. Counted by id,
  #4471 holds **412** reports.
- Split by cause: **379** parser + **33** hint = 412.
- Five reports the desk read as a one-day move are still parser by cause; they are footnoted,
  not split out.

## Resolved (desk, #4471 closed 05 Oct)

- **parser — FIXED.** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket
  [#1](https://github.com/paulklecha/mega-dev-assignments/issues/1) closed as completed.
- **hint — WON'T FIX.** booking-v3 form retired, so the form-hint bug goes away with the form.
  Ticket [#2](https://github.com/paulklecha/mega-dev-assignments/issues/2) closed as not planned.

## Lessons

- Merging on subject is fast, but it buries a second bug with the same symptom. Re-read the
  merge when a "known" ticket keeps growing.
- A number that can be computed should be computed. The intake tag disagreed with the cause on
  38 reports; trusting it would have split the counts wrong.

